== forecast_help ==
usage: revenue_forecast.py [-h] [--output OUTPUT] [--markdown MARKDOWN]
                           [--validate-only] [--verbose] [--version]
                           [input]

Calculate a source-traceable revenue-only forecast

positional arguments:
  input                input JSON document (required unless --version)

options:
  -h, --help           show this help message and exit
  --output OUTPUT      JSON output path; stdout when omitted
  --markdown MARKDOWN  optional Markdown report path
  --validate-only      validate input and output without writing
  --verbose            with --validate-only, report every input violation in
                       one pass
  --version            print engine version and this installation's manifest
                       hash (R4.2)

== generator_help ==
usage: generate_input_template.py [-h] --name NAME --base-year BASE_YEAR
                                  --forecast-years FORECAST_YEARS [FORECAST_YEARS ...]
                                  [--currency CURRENCY] [--unit UNIT]
                                  --segments SEGMENTS [SEGMENTS ...]
                                  [--output OUTPUT]
                                  [--segment-model SEGMENT=MODEL]
                                  [--schema VERSION]

Emit a schema input skeleton pre-filled with correct field names.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --name NAME           company name
  --base-year BASE_YEAR
                        base fiscal year (e.g. 2025)
  --forecast-years FORECAST_YEARS [FORECAST_YEARS ...]
                        forecast years (e.g. 2026 2027)
  --currency CURRENCY   currency code (default USD)
  --unit UNIT           monetary unit (default million)
  --segments SEGMENTS [SEGMENTS ...]
                        segment display names
  --output OUTPUT       write skeleton here (default stdout)
  --segment-model SEGMENT=MODEL
                        select a registered revenue model for a segment;
                        repeat for multiple segments
  --schema VERSION      opt-in schema version (default 3.7; 3.8 adds
                        operating_units, 3.9 adds dated period flows and role-
                        aware triangulation)

== source_help ==
usage: source_preparation.py [-h] [--request-file REQUEST_FILE]
                             [--allow-download] [--result-envelope]
                             [--narrative-request-file NARRATIVE_REQUEST_FILE]
                             [--source-reader-v2]
                             [--company-wiki-catalog-config COMPANY_WIKI_CATALOG_CONFIG]
                             [--source-reader-receipt-version {2.1,2.2}]
                             [--timeout-seconds TIMEOUT_SECONDS]
                             [--company-wiki-config COMPANY_WIKI_CONFIG]
                             [--filing-fetch-root FILING_FETCH_ROOT]

Revenue source preparation — the single production entry.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --request-file REQUEST_FILE
                        request JSON file (else stdin)
  --allow-download
  --result-envelope     retain filing-fetch result and explicit narrative read
                        receipt
  --narrative-request-file NARRATIVE_REQUEST_FILE
                        explicit existing narrative-read-request/1 or
                        projected /3; never starts a model
  --source-reader-v2    compatibility no-op: SourceRef v2 is the only default;
                        the legacy normalized-body reader is no longer
                        reachable
  --company-wiki-catalog-config COMPANY_WIKI_CATALOG_CONFIG
  --source-reader-receipt-version {2.1,2.2}
                        declared producer receipt capability; 2.2 explicitly
                        requests availability evidence
  --timeout-seconds TIMEOUT_SECONDS
  --company-wiki-config COMPANY_WIKI_CONFIG
                        override company-wiki config for the chain (E2E)
  --filing-fetch-root FILING_FETCH_ROOT
                        override the filing-fetch skill root for the chain
                        (E2E)

== support_help ==
usage: research_support_diagnostics.py [-h] --input INPUT [--output OUTPUT]

Read-only economic support diagnostics over one native forecast input.

options:
  -h, --help       show this help message and exit
  --input INPUT    Path to the native forecast input JSON (read-only).
  --output OUTPUT  New output path for the diagnostics JSON; omit to print to
                   stdout. Existing files are not overwritten.

== snapshot_help ==
usage: revenue_backtest.py create [-h] --version VERSION --output OUTPUT input

positional arguments:
  input

options:
  -h, --help         show this help message and exit
  --version VERSION
  --output OUTPUT

== lint_help ==
usage: lint_input.py [-h] [--check-conclusion-facts]
                     [--check-sensitivity-propagation]
                     input

Collect-all static pre-flight linter for schema inputs.

positional arguments:
  input                 input JSON path (see
                        contracts.constants.FORECAST_SCHEMA_VERSION)

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --check-conclusion-facts
                        warn when a coverage conclusion contains digits with
                        no claim backing (heuristic, opt-in)
  --check-sensitivity-propagation
                        warn when a sensitivity shocks an absolute-level
                        driver before the terminal year (heuristic, opt-in)

== hash_help ==
usage: fix_hashes.py [-h] [--output OUTPUT] [--check] [--dry-run] input

Recompute and sync schema input-side hashes.

positional arguments:
  input            input JSON path (see
                   contracts.constants.FORECAST_SCHEMA_VERSION)

options:
  -h, --help       show this help message and exit
  --output OUTPUT  write fixed JSON here instead of in place
  --check          report drift only, write nothing (exit 2 on drift)
  --dry-run        print planned fixes, write nothing

